## Review scoring rules

### Input — each review arrives with this schema

```json
{
  "review_id":             "string — unique identifier",
  "position":              "integer — order in the list (1 = most recent)",
  "rating":                "integer — 1 to 5",
  "snippet":               "string — review text",
  "snippet_length":        "integer — character count of snippet",
  "author_name":           "string",
  "author_reviews_count":  "integer — total reviews by this author on Google Maps",
  "author_photos_count":   "integer — total photos uploaded by this author",
  "is_local_guide":        "boolean",
  "images_count":          "integer — photos attached to this review",
  "response_present":      "boolean — owner replied to this review",
  "was_edited":            "boolean — review was modified after posting",
  "likes":                 "integer — helpful votes from other users"
}
```

### Output — for each review return a scored object

For every review, go through EVERY row of both scoring tables below — in order, one by one.
For each row: answer the Check question. If YES → add the key to `score_breakdown`. If NO → skip it.
Do not stop early. Do not skip rows. Process all 25 signals for every review.

The example below shows the structure only. Any key from the scoring table above may appear:

```json
{
  "review_id": "string",
  "rating": "integer (1–5)",
  "author_name": "string",
  "score_breakdown": [
    { "key": "THIN_ACCOUNT_1",      "value": 10 },
    { "key": "SHORT_TEXT",          "value": 10 },
    { "key": "GENERIC_TEXT",        "value": 20 },
    { "key": "FIVE_STAR_EMPTY",     "value": 15 },
    { "key": "EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5","value": -10 }
  ]
}
```

---

## Scoring table

### Fake signals — add points

| Key                    | Points | Description | Check |
|------------------------|--------|-------------|-------|
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_0`       | +20    | Author has 0–1 total reviews on Google Maps | author_reviews_count ≤ 1? |
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_1`       | +10    | Author has 2–3 total reviews on Google Maps | author_reviews_count 2–3? |
| `SHORT_TEXT_EXTREME`   | +25    | Review text under 20 characters | snippet_length < 20? |
| `SHORT_TEXT`           | +10    | Review text under 40 characters | snippet_length < 40? |
| `BURST_AFTER_NEGATIVE` | +20    | 5★ review within 5 positions after a 1–2★ review | Is this 5★ review within 5 positions after a 1–2★ review in the list? |
| `FIVE_STAR_EMPTY`      | +15    | 5★ rating with text under 50 characters | rating = 5 AND snippet_length < 50? |
| `SURNAME_REPEAT`       | +20    | Reviewer shares last name with another reviewer in the same set | Does another reviewer in this set share the same last name? |
| `GENERIC_TEXT`         | +20    | **Absence of specifics** — no repair type, no product, no price, no staff name, no waiting time, no concrete situation described. The review could have been written by someone who was never there. | After reading the snippet, can you answer at least ONE of: (a) exactly what service/product/repair was performed; (b) an exact price; (c) an exact wait time; (d) a staff member's name; (e) a specific physical detail? If you cannot → apply |
| `SUSPICIOUS_NEGATIVE`  | +20    | 1–2★ review combined with thin account, short text, or generic content | rating 1–2 AND (author thin OR text short OR no specific incident described)? |
| `MARKETING_TONE`       | +10    | **Promotional or exaggerated language** — superlatives, emotional filler: "best ever", "incredible", "world-class". The review sounds like an ad. | Does the text read like an ad — superlatives, emotional filler, "best ever", "world-class"? |
| `ALL_POSITIVE`         | +15    | **Only positives, zero negatives or caveats** — nothing but praise with no minor criticism, no nuance, no "but". | Read every sentence. Is there zero negative words, zero caveats ("but", "however", "though", "хотя", "но"), and zero neutral observations? Even one mild criticism disqualifies. |
| `NO_FIRST_PERSON`      | +5     | **No first-person voice** — no "I", "me", "my", "we", "я", "мы", "мне". Written from the outside, not as a personal experience. | Is there no "I / me / my / we / our / я / мне / мой / мы / наш" anywhere in the text? |
| `FUTURE_PROMISE`       | +5     | **Future promise without past detail** — "will return", "теперь только сюда" without describing what happened. | Does the text promise to return or recommend without describing what actually happened? |
| `BUSINESS_NAME_DROP`   | +10    | **Explicitly names the business in the review text**. Real reviewers rarely type the full business name. | Does the text contain the actual business name from place_data (not "this place", "here", or pronouns)? |
| `EMOJI_SPAM`           | +10    | Excessive punctuation or decorative emoji with no informational content | Excessive emoji or !!!-punctuation with no informational content? |
| `TEMPLATE_CLONE`       | +20    | Phrasing nearly identical to another review in the same set | Is the phrasing nearly identical to another review in this set? |
| `REPEATABLE_PLUSES_2`  | +5     | **Exactly 2 distinct praise phrases** in one review. Stacked praise without substance. | Count distinct praise phrases. Are there exactly 2? |
| `REPEATABLE_PLUSES_3`  | +5     | **3 or more distinct praise phrases** in one review. Stacks with REPEATABLE_PLUSES_2 (+10 total). | Count distinct praise phrases. Are there 3 or more? |

### Real signals — subtract points

| Key                     | Points | Description | Check |
|-------------------------|--------|-------------|-------|
| `EDITED_REVIEW`         | −5     | Review was edited after initial posting | was_edited = true? |
| `HAS_PHOTOS`            | −10    | Review includes attached photos | images_count > 0? |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5`  | −5     | Author has more than 5 reviews on Google Maps | author_reviews_count ≥ 5? |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_10` | −10    | Author has more than 10 reviews on Google Maps | author_reviews_count ≥ 10? |
| `ACTIVE_PROFILE`        | −5     | Author has uploaded more than 5 photos to Google Maps | author_photos_count > 5? |
| `LONG_TEXT`             | −10    | Review text over 400 characters | snippet_length > 400? |
| `SPECIFIC_DETAILS`      | −10    | Mentions specific names, prices, waiting times, or physical details | Does the text mention a specific person's name, an exact price amount, an exact duration, a specific part/product name, or a concrete physical description? Generic words like "service", "defects", "quality", "everything" do NOT count. |
| `BALANCED_TONE`         | −10    | Review notes both positives and negatives or caveats | Does the text include both positives and at least one negative or caveat? |
| `NATURAL_LANGUAGE`      | −10    | Informal language, typos, colloquialisms, personal voice | Does the text have typos, informal phrasing, or a personal voice? |
| `LOCAL_GUIDE`           | −3     | Author is a Google-verified Local Guide | is_local_guide = true? |
| `OWNER_RESPONDED`       | −3     | The business owner replied to this review | response_present = true? |
| `HELPFUL_VOTES`         | −10    | Other users marked this review as helpful | likes > 0? |
